	<!-- wp:group {"tagName":"section","anchor":"faq","align":"wide","className":"wcr-faq wcr-rail","layout":{"type":"default"}} -->
	<section class="wp-block-group alignwide wcr-faq wcr-rail" id="faq">
		<!-- wp:columns {"className":"wcr-faq__grid"} -->
		<div class="wp-block-columns wcr-faq__grid">
			<!-- wp:column {"width":"34%"} -->
			<div class="wp-block-column" style="flex-basis:34%"><!-- wp:group {"className":"wcr-faq__intro","layout":{"type":"default"}} -->
			<div class="wp-block-group wcr-faq__intro"><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"wcr-kicker"} --><p class="wcr-kicker">QUESTIONS, ANSWERED</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading {"className":"wcr-section-title"} --><h2 class="wp-block-heading wcr-section-title">Everything you need<br><em>before you start.</em></h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"wcr-faq__lede"} --><p class="wcr-faq__lede">Straight answers about collecting, managing, and displaying richer WooCommerce reviews.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>
			<!-- /wp:group --></div>
			<!-- /wp:column -->

			<!-- wp:column {"width":"66%"} -->
			<div class="wp-block-column" style="flex-basis:66%"><!-- wp:group {"className":"wcr-faq-list","layout":{"type":"default"}} -->
			<div class="wp-block-group wcr-faq-list">
				<!-- wp:details {"className":"wcr-faq-item"} -->
				<details class="wp-block-details wcr-faq-item" open><summary>Does this replace WooCommerce reviews?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>No. It enhances the standard WooCommerce product-review system. Reviews continue to use WordPress comments and the familiar WooCommerce moderation workflow.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
				<!-- /wp:details -->

				<!-- wp:details {"className":"wcr-faq-item"} -->
				<details class="wp-block-details wcr-faq-item"><summary>Do customers need an app to record video?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>No. On supported browsers, customers can grant camera and microphone access and record directly from the product page. They can upload an existing video when browser recording is unavailable.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
				<!-- /wp:details -->

				<!-- wp:details {"className":"wcr-faq-item"} -->
				<details class="wp-block-details wcr-faq-item"><summary>Which video formats are supported?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Customers can upload MP4, WebM, and MKV files. Browser recordings use the video format supported by the customer’s browser, with a configurable maximum length from 1 to 10 minutes.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
				<!-- /wp:details -->

				<!-- wp:details {"className":"wcr-faq-item"} -->
				<details class="wp-block-details wcr-faq-item"><summary>Can video and photo uploads be optional?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Yes. Webcam recording, video uploads, and photo uploads can be enabled independently. Video recording or video-file upload can also be required before a review is submitted.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
				<!-- /wp:details -->

				<!-- wp:details {"className":"wcr-faq-item"} -->
				<details class="wp-block-details wcr-faq-item"><summary>How are verified customers identified?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The verified-customer badge uses WooCommerce’s verified-owner check for the review and associated purchase, so it appears only for confirmed owners.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
				<!-- /wp:details -->

				<!-- wp:details {"className":"wcr-faq-item"} -->
				<details class="wp-block-details wcr-faq-item"><summary>How do automated review reminders work?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Create one or more rules with their own order-status trigger, delay, subject, and message. Each rule sends at most once per order, and customers can unsubscribe from future requests.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
				<!-- /wp:details -->

				<!-- wp:details {"className":"wcr-faq-item"} -->
				<details class="wp-block-details wcr-faq-item"><summary>Can I display reviews on another page?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Yes. Open ReviQuo → Review Shortcode, create a named display, and place its generated shortcode—such as <code>[reviquo id="123"]</code>—in any shortcode-compatible page, post, or builder.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
				<!-- /wp:details -->
			</div>
			<!-- /wp:group --></div>
			<!-- /wp:column -->
		</div>
		<!-- /wp:columns -->
	</section>
	<!-- /wp:group -->

